### I CANNOT SOLVE THIS

Artin's conjecture on primitive roots is a genuine open problem in number theory. The unconditional version (`artin_primitive_roots.parts.i`) is open — no proof is known without assuming GRH. The conditional version (`conditional_artin_primitive_roots.parts.i`) depends on the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis, which is itself one of the Millennium Prize open problems (and is imported here via `FormalConjectures.Millenium.RiemannHypothesis`). Since GRH is unproved, even the "conditional" theorem cannot be unconditionally established, and formalizing Hooley's GRH-conditional argument would itself require building substantial machinery (character sums, sieve density estimates, entanglement field theory) that is far beyond what can be produced here.

